/E (Given these differences, regulatory strategies should prioritize enforceable frontend product-level mandates where possible, as they offer greater assurance of compliance and user benefit. At the same time, regulators should develop and require transparency frameworks and independent audit mechanisms to hold platforms accountable for backend algorithmic changes. This dual approach reflects emerging regulatory practices seen in the UK Age-Appropriate Design Code and the EU Digital Services Act, which combine visible interface restrictions with demands for algorithmic disclosures and audit access.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
